 "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"int